[{"id":117429,"sender_id":1169,"sender_full_name":"Shamrock","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d9ccb05a18035ca5b5a1a126bd61e8bd?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/ind-object.20in.20an.20.28infinity.2C1.29-category/near/117429\">#1</a> On the page “ind-object in an (infinity,1)-category” there’s a section “In terms of formal colimits” which is left as a stub with “(… should be made more precise…)”. Does anyone know if this has been made precise anywhere, in any model of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty, 1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-categories? I’ve only ever seen colimit completions of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty, 1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-categories defined in terms of presheaves. In general it’s harder to give “objects &amp; morphisms” definitions of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty, 1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-categories.</p>","timestamp":1727472604,"subject":"ind-object in an (infinity,1)-category","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":117431,"sender_id":563,"sender_full_name":"Hurkyl","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ff42efa94f111c3f310350c872de031d?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/ind-object.20in.20an.20.28infinity.2C1.29-category/near/117431\">#2</a> For what it’s worth, I consider the presheaf version to be precisely the way to make it more precise; you can easily verify that it has the right hom-spaces:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≃</mo><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></munder><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≃</mo><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></munder><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">colim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></munder><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"> \\widehat{C}(\\mathrm{colim}_i C(-, F_i), \\mathrm{colim}_j C(-, G_j)) \\simeq \\lim_i \\widehat{C}(C(-, F_i), \\mathrm{colim}_j C(-, G_j)) \\simeq \\lim_i \\operatorname*{colim}_j C(F_i, G_j) </annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2094em;vertical-align:-0.286